reply:
{"question": "Group events disappear after updating group properties
After I update a group's metadata through the API, some of that group's previously captured events vanish from my analytics dashboards. The events were recorded before the property update and should still be visible. This happens consistently whenever I modify group properties.

Expected: Updating group properties should not affect the visibility of historical events associated with that group.","gold_fqn":"posthog.models.group.group.Group"}

{"question": "Salesforce lookup returns no record even when one exists
When I look up a contact by email and there is exactly one matching record, the lookup step reports that nothing was found — the returned ID and record fields are both empty. If two records match, it still returns the second one instead of the first. I expected the lookup to return the first matching record.

I set up the Salesforce destination integration, configured it to search the Contact object on the Email field, and triggered it with an event where the person had an email address. The step always failed to surface the correct contact.", "gold_fqn": "posthog.cdp.templates.salesforce.template_salesforce.template_lookup"}

{"question": "Duplicate actions when clicking Slack buttons
When I click a button or submit a modal in Slack, the associated action sometimes runs twice. I don't always see it — it seems to happen when there's a brief network hiccup between Slack and our server. I expected each interaction to be processed exactly once.

The Events API endpoint correctly uses Slack's event ID for deduplication, but the interactivity endpoint never provides a delivery identifier, so retried requests slip through as new deliveries.", "gold_fqn": "posthog.ingress.slack.provider.SlackInteractivityProvider.deliveries"}

{"question": "Setting replacement behavior to zero disables it instead of enabling it
When I pass 0 as the replacement setting, the paths feature behaves as if replacements are turned off, even though 0 should be treated differently from a missing or null value. I expected that passing an explicit numeric value like 0 would either enable replacements or at least not silently collapse to false.

gold_fqn": "posthog.models.filters.mixins.paths.PathReplacementMixin.path_replacements"}

{"question": "Web experiments disappear after saving
When I create a new web experiment through the web experiments interface and save it, it doesn't appear in my web experiments list afterward. It only shows up if I switch to the general experiments view. I expected newly created web experiments to remain visible in the web experiments list.

", "gold_fqn": "products.experiments.backend.models.web_experiment.WebExperiment"}

{"question": "Usage reports fail when CDP delivery counts are measured
When I run usage reports for an org that has hog function destinations configured, the entire billing report crashes with an error about unpacking too many values. The error occurs during the CDP delivery metrics collection step. I expected the report to succeed and show my destination invocation counts.

The best place to look is the function that queries hog function call metrics from app_metrics2 — it groups by both team_id and metric_name but the caller expects two-column tuples.", "gold_fqn": "posthog.tasks.usage_report.get_teams_with_hog_function_calls_in_period"}

{"question": "Entry hostname property returns no values
When I query for distinct values of the entry hostname session property, I get an empty list even though sessions clearly have hostnames. The same happens for end hostname. These properties appear in the session schema and show up in queries, but the property value explorer shows nothing.

e.g. when browsing session property dropdowns or using the API to fetch available values for entry hostname, the result is always blank despite other entry properties like entry URL and entry pathname returning values correctly.", "gold_fqn": "posthog.hogql.database.schema.sessions_v2.get_lazy_session_table_values_v2"}

{"question": "Dashboard still shows old issue status after refresh
I updated an issue's status to "resolved" and immediately refreshed the error tracking dashboard, but the issue still displayed its previous status. This happened on a team with many issues being updated around the same time. I expected the dashboard to always reflect the most recent state after a refresh.

gold_fqn": "products.error_tracking.backend.hogql_queries.issue_state_overlay.load_recent_issue_states"}

{"question": "Route labels inconsistent in rate limit metrics
When I check our Prometheus dashboards for rate limit data, the same API endpoint appears under two different route labels — one with a trailing slash and one without. For example, /api/projects/TEAM_ID/ and /api/projects/TEAM_ID show up as separate entries. This fragments our metrics and makes it impossible to aggregate requests per endpoint accurately.

The issue stems from how the route identifier is built: the function strips the regex anchors but leaves a trailing slash when the URL pattern includes one, while stripping it when the pattern does not. Since Django's URL patterns may or may not include a trailing slash depending on how they are defined, the resulting label depends on the route definition rather than the actual endpoint.", "gold_fqn": "posthog.rate_limit.replace_with_param_names"}

{"question": "Column aliases in CTEs with UNION don't apply to all branches
When I define a CTE that wraps a UNION and provide an explicit column name list, only the first branch of the union gets the renamed columns. The other branches keep their original column names, so referencing the CTE can produce ambiguous or unexpected results.

Example: WITH cte(a, b) AS (SELECT x AS a, y AS b FROM t1 UNION ALL SELECT p AS a, q AS b FROM t2) — the second branch still exposes columns named p and q instead of a and b.","gold_fqn": "posthog.hogql.resolver.visit_cte"}

{"question": "Cohort calculation crashes when a referenced dynamic cohort has been deleted
When I try to calculate a cohort that includes a dynamic cohort condition, the calculation fails with a database error if the referenced dynamic cohort was deleted after the cohort was originally configured. Static cohorts that are deleted behave differently—the calculation completes and simply returns zero members. Dynamic cohorts, however, cause the entire cohort calculation to crash. I expected both types to fail gracefully and return an empty result when the referenced cohort no longer exists.

The calculation was triggered by viewing a cohort's member list after a referenced dynamic cohort had been removed from the system.", "gold_fqn": "posthog.hogql_queries.hogql_cohort_query.HogQLCohortQuery.get_dynamic_cohort_condition"}

{"question": "Duplicate billing records appear in reports
I noticed that the same usage event shows up multiple times in our billing summary even though we only sent it once. When I check the raw data the record_id is identical but there are several rows with slightly different timestamps. I expected ClickHouse's deduplication to keep only the latest version of each record.

gold_fqn": "posthog.models.usage_ingestion.billing_usage_records.billing_usage_records_data_table_engine"}

{"question": "Root message status line stays stale after resolving an issue
When I resolve an issue, the reply thread says it's resolved but the root message still shows the old active status. It doesn't update until another lifecycle event happens later. I expected the root to reflect the new status right away.

The root status only gets updated when a subsequent reply triggers a check against the database, but at that point the database has already been updated. If no other events fire in between, the root remains stuck on the old status indefinitely.", "gold_fqn": "products.error_tracking.backend.temporal.alerts.delivery._reconcile_root_status"}

{"question": "After a force-push, reading ownership files stays slow for hours
A developer force-pushed a branch, which made the diff between the old and new head unprovable. After that, every page load for our repo does a full read of all ownership files instead of reusing unchanged entries. The slowdown persists for over 24 hours, even though normal commits followed and the comparison should be provable again. I expected the reuse optimization to resume once the heads were in a linear relationship.

gold_fqn": "posthog.ownership.github_files.AuthenticatedRepoFiles._unchanged_since_previous_head"}

{"question": "Running queries list hides queries that reference pg_stat_activity
When I check the running queries page, my own query disappears from the list if it happens to mention the pg_stat_activity table. I was running SELECT * FROM pg_stat_activity LIMIT 10 to check active connections, and it did not appear in the running queries view even though it was executing. I expected all queries longer than a few seconds to show up regardless of what tables they touch.

The filter meant to exclude the monitoring query itself is too broad and also excludes legitimate queries that reference pg_stat_activity.", "gold_fqn": "posthog.api.instance_status.InstanceStatusViewSet.get_postgres_running_queries"}

{"question": "Funnel experiment breakdown values are wrong when using the optimized query path
When I run a funnel experiment with a breakdown (like browser or source) and the optimized query path is used, the breakdown column shows incorrect groupings — some events appear under the wrong breakdown value. The same experiment works correctly with the non-optimized query. I expected the optimized path to produce identical breakdown results.

gold_fqn": "products.experiments.backend.hogql_queries.breakdown_injector.inject_funnel_breakdown_columns_optimized"}

{"question": "Authentication fails during identity provider key rotation
After our SSO provider rotated its signing keys, login stopped working for several hours even though the ID token was perfectly valid. The error said the token or JWKS was invalid, but other tools could verify it fine. Once the old key was fully removed from the provider's JWKS endpoint, authentication started working again.

We expect authentication to succeed as long as the token was signed by a currently trusted key, even if multiple RSA signing keys are published in the JWKS during the transition period.", "gold_fqn": "posthog.api.oidc.MultitenantOIDCAuth.find_valid_key"}
